PropStruct is a port to C# of PropStructV3, a Fortran program for modelling the structure
of composite solid rocket propellants ("Программа моделирования структуры СТРТ"), by
V. A. Babuk and A. A. Nizyaev, Baltic State Technical University "VOENMEH" named after
D. F. Ustinov (Saint Petersburg). The model is described in V. A. Babuk and A. A.
Nizyaev, "Modelling of structure of the composite solid propellants and problem of the
description of agglomeration process", Khimicheskaya Fizika i Mezoskopiya (Chemical
Physics and Mesoscopy), 2014, vol. 16, no. 1, pp. 31-42. The original program's source
code and executable are not distributed with PropStruct.

PropStruct depends on ILGPU (University of Illinois/NCSA Open Source License) and does not
redistribute it. PropStruct.Cli does: it bundles ILGPU.dll, and ILGPU's licence is in
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt in that package.
